OL,3,GNEWSAHundreds of tenants face care
OL,4,Aalarm price hike
OL,5,
OL,6,FElderly and disabled residents in
OL,7,Findependent living accommodation in
OL,8,FSheffield face paying an extra #11 a
OL,9,Fmonth for an alarm service which
OL,10,Fprovides emergency help.
OL,12,FSheffield City Council is planning to
OL,13,Fincrease the charge for the City Wide
OL,14,FCare Alarm service for tenants in the
OL,15,FOlder Persons Independent Living
OL,16,Fservice.
OL,18,FTenants in this type of accommodation,
OL,19,Fsuch as extra care and sheltered
OL,20,Fhousing, cannot opt out and must pay
OL,21,Fthe charge as part of their tenancy
OL,22,Fagreement.
OL,23,APub: 23-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
